# Netlify redirect rules. This file lives in the publish root (netlify.toml sets
# publish = "."), which is deliberate: redirects declared in netlify.toml have
# been dropped silently on this account before, while _redirects is reliable.
#
# Hosted invite links. convex/events.ts mints https://mixandgreet.com/i/<slug>
# and rsvp.html resolves the key from either the path or ?event=. The 200 makes
# this a REWRITE rather than a redirect, so the pretty URL stays in the address
# bar and in link previews. Without this rule every minted invite link 404s.
/i/*    /rsvp.html?event=:splat    200

# The brand-side questionnaire. Same 200 rewrite as /i/* and for the same
# reason: the URL that gets emailed to a brand partner is
# mixandgreet.com/brand-interest, and it has to stay that in the address bar.
# (www.mixandgreet.com 301s to the apex at the DNS/Netlify layer, so the
# www form of the link lands here too.)
/brand-interest    /brand-interest.html    200

# The two back-office rooms that are not about one evening: the CRM, and the
# partnership pipeline. Same 200 rewrite, and here the pretty URL is doing a
# second job as well as reading better: /admin.html links to them by these
# names, and a staff member who has bookmarked one should not be holding a URL
# that changes if the file behind it is ever renamed. Both are noindex and both
# sit behind the same token gate as /admin.html; the rewrite makes them
# reachable, not public.
/crm               /crm.html               200
/partnerships      /partnerships.html      200
